  "name": "HEPATITIS C VIRUS (HCV) GENOTYPE",
  "code": "HCVGEN",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"190\" data-end=\"297\">\n<p data-start=\"192\" data-end=\"297\">HCV exists in <strong data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"294\">different genetic variants (genotypes 1&ndash;6, with multiple subtypes: 1a, 1b, 2a, etc.)</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"298\" data-end=\"510\">\n<p data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"389\">The genotype does <strong data-start=\"318\" data-end=\"354\">not affect the risk of infection</strong>, but it plays a crucial role in:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"392\" data-end=\"510\">\n<li data-start=\"392\" data-end=\"426\">\n<p data-start=\"394\" data-end=\"426\"><strong data-start=\"394\" data-end=\"424\">Choosing antiviral therapy</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"429\" data-end=\"470\">\n<p data-start=\"431\" data-end=\"470\"><strong data-start=\"431\" data-end=\"468\">Determining duration of treatment</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"473\" data-end=\"510\">\n<p data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"510\"><strong>Predicting treatment response</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Genotype Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Genotype 1 (1a or 1b)</strong></td>\n<td>Most common worldwide. Historically had lower response to older therapies, but with Direct-Acting Antivirals (DAAs), cure rates are very high. Some regimens still adjust dose/duration based on subtype.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Genotype 2</strong></td>\n<td>Generally responds very well to therapy; shorter treatment durations may be effective.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Genotype 3</strong></td>\n<td>Common in South Asia. Associated with more rapid progression of liver fibrosis and fatty liver. Requires specific antiviral regimens and sometimes longer treatment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Genotype 4</strong></td>\n<td>Common in the Middle East and Africa. Responds well to modern DAAs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Genotype 5 &amp; 6</strong></td>\n<td>Less common; found in parts of South Africa and Southeast Asia. Usually sensitive to pan-genotypic therapies.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mixed Genotype</strong></td>\n<td>Infection with more than one genotype. Therapy should be guided by pan-genotypic antivirals.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>No genotype detected</strong></td>\n<td>May occur if HCV RNA level is below the detection limit or infection has resolved.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
